[Nabladown.js](https://github.com/pedroth/nabladown.js) is a parser and renderer for the `nabladown.js` language, which is a pseudo/flavored *Markdown* language.

I made [Nabladown.js](https://github.com/pedroth/nabladown.js) because I wanted a simple way to render *HTML documents* with *formulas*, *code highlighting*, *media*, etc. These are the main features of the language:

- Simple language, like *Markdown*.
- Supports *mathematical formulas* (_LaTeX style_).
- Supports *code highlighting*.
- Supports regular *HTML*.
- Supports [*macros*][macros].
- Exposes the *parser* of the language.
- Easy way to write multiple *renderers*.
- Easy to install and use.

The main motivation for [Nabladown.js](https://github.com/pedroth/nabladown.js) was rendering the posts on this website.

Please check the project page for more details.

